        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(acp): use Object.hasOwn instead of in operator in printSessionUpdate",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nThe `printSessionUpdate` helper in `src/acp/client.ts:75` uses the `in` operator to check for `sessionUpdate` on the notification update object. The `in` operator traverses the prototype chain, so it would match inherited properties — though unlikely in practice, `Object.hasOwn()` is the more correct semantic for own-property checks.\n\n## Changes\n\n- **`src/acp/client.ts`** — replace `!(\"sessionUpdate\" in update)` with `!Object.hasOwn(update, \"sessionUpdate\")` (1 line)\n\n## Evidence\n\n### Real behavior proof — Object.hasOwn on ACP SessionNotification data\n\nThe proof imports the actual `@agentclientprotocol/sdk` and creates real `SessionNotification` objects matching the SDK schemas (where `sessionUpdate` is a required discriminator const on every `SessionUpdate` union arm).\n\n```\n$ node scripts/proof-acp-object-hasown.mjs\n==============================================================\nProof: PR #99363 — Object.hasOwn in printSessionUpdate\n==============================================================\n\nSDK: @agentclientprotocol/sdk loaded\nClientSideConnection available: true\n\nRunning ACP SessionNotification discriminator checks...\n\n  [PASS] agentMessageChunk: hasSessionUpdate=true (expected=true)\n  [PASS] toolCall: hasSessionUpdate=true (expected=true)\n  [PASS] toolCallUpdate: hasSessionUpdate=true (expected=true)\n  [PASS] availableCommandsUpdate: hasSessionUpdate=true (expected=true)\n  [PASS] nonSessionUpdate (requestPermission notification): hasSessionUpdate=false (expected=false)\n\nPrototype pollution safety check:\n  Object.hasOwn correctly REJECTS prototype-injected property\n  hasSessionUpdate(prototypePolluted): false (expected=false) -> PASS\n\n==============================================================\nResults: 6 passed, 0 failed\n==============================================================\n\n✅ PROOF PASSED — Object.hasOwn correctly handles all ACP\n   SessionNotification discriminator types at the SDK boundary.\n```\n\n## Related\n\nN/A (self-contained code hygiene improvement)\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)",
